From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:43:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: Generate mipmaps with the compute shader on
 KosmicKrisp.

KosmicKrisp blits through a Metal render pass of its own, so a mip chain
cost a render pass per level, recorded on the CS thread. Kebab Chefs
generates about 110 levels per frame in its main menu; with one compute
dispatch per chain it runs at 50 instead of 29 fps.

The shader samples levels that do not halve exactly at slightly
different positions than a blit, which docs/macos/d3d11-mipgen.c in
MacProton takes into account.
---
 src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
index bd8ad03..87a0e41 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device.cpp
@@ -739,9 +739,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // Compute-based mip generation has some potential for performance
     // regressions or driver issues. Just enable it on Nvidia and RADV
     // (GFX10+) for now, where it is proven to work.
+    // KosmicKrisp starts a Metal render pass for every blit, and a mip chain
+    // costs it one per level.
     hints.preferComputeMipGen = (m_adapter->matchesDriver(VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY_KHR)
                              || (m_adapter->matchesDriver(VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_RADV)
-                              && m_properties.vk13.minSubgroupSize == 32u));
+                              && m_properties.vk13.minSubgroupSize == 32u)
+                             || m_adapter->matchesDriver(VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP));
 
     // On AMD we can expect it to be optimal to simply pass the heap offset
     // to descriptor memory through as-is to avoid some ALU. Some other
